<title>USA: TABLE - Intl Paper Q2 loss after charges.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Intl Paper Q2 loss after charges.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $1.39   profit	 $0.33</p>
<p> Net loss		 419,000   profit	99,000</p>
<p> Net sales	    5,000,000		5,100,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 301,100		  299,100</p>
<p>	  6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $1.28   profit	 $0.69</p>
<p> Net loss		 385,000   profit     197,000</p>
<p> Net sales	    9,900,000		9,900,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 300,900		  284,000</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Both 1997 periods include $535 million pre-tax business improvement reserve ($385 million after taxes, or $1.28 per share), and $150 million pre-tax legal reserve ($93 million after taxes, or $0.31 per share).</p>
<p>Excluding charges, 1997 Q2 earnings were $59 million, or $0.20 per share.</p>
<p>1996 six months includes $515 million pre-tax restructuring charge ($362 million after taxes, or $1.35 per share), and $592 million pre-tax gain ($336 million after taxes, or $1.25 per share) on the sale of a partnership interest.</p>
<p>Full name is International Paper Co.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
